draw from your station table.

112
00:09:00.965 --> 00:09:05.052
Watch the core stream being built station
by station from the computed totals:

113
00:09:05.092 --> 00:09:09.570
first the free ram compression from the
static free-stream to the total state.

114
00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:14.674
Then the fan and the two compressors
climb to 771 kelvin, each

115
00:09:14.714 --> 00:09:18.654
process drifting to the right
because losses generate entropy.

116
00:09:18.704 --> 00:09:22.952
The burner adds heat up to 1
600 kelvin at slightly falling

117
00:09:22.992 --> 00:09:28.179
pressure, and the two turbines
expand the gas down to 1 046 kelvin.

118
00:09:28.229 --> 00:09:32.899
Finally the nozzle accelerates the
flow to its choked exit at 909

119
00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:37.658
kelvin static, and the vertical extent
of the diagram is bounded by T t four.

120
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:41.030
Two cautions for the sketch:
this is an open trace of total

121
00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:44.562
states with losses, not a closed
reversible cycle, so the area

122
00:09:44.602 --> 00:09:48.208
under or inside it is not the net
work; and the bypass stream is

123
00:09:48.248 --> 00:09:52.196
a separate short branch, from 2
to 13 through the fan and then

124
00:09:52.236 --> 00:09:57.087
